 "notes": "Headline curve = green 'Stochastic' line of Fig. 3 (file modifiedVULFexclusionCombined2CORRECTED2.pdf in the e-print), the paper's stochastic-corrected 95% CL exclusion on the axion-nucleon gradient coupling g_aNN [GeV^-1], combining the corrected nEDM (Abel 2017), CASPEr-ZULF-Comagnetometer (Wu 2019, corrected by factor ~8.4) and CASPEr-ZULF-Sideband (Garcon 2019, re-derived and rescaled 90%->95% CL) limits. This is the paper's own re-derivation (Bayesian stochastic treatment) of previously published data, not a new measurement; the corrected curve is the paper's main quantitative result. Vector paths extracted with exact tick calibration (x: -22..-13 log10 m_phi/eV, y: -6..-1 log10 g_aNN/GeV^-1); black new-force line reproduces the quoted ~1e-4 GeV^-1. Converted to canonical dimensionless g_an = 2 m_n * g_aNN[GeV^-1] with m_n = 0.93957 GeV (2m_N rule for H = g grad(a).sigma_N). Curve has a real gap between ~1.3e-17 and ~2.1e-16 eV where the DM experiments give no constraint (only the mass-independent K-3He new-force bound applies there). Assumed rho_DM ~= 0.4 GeV/cm^3.",
